file crates/gui/src/widgets/code.rs
symbol code_block
lines 0 93
hash a07e2aa176e811fd
note The one code element in the GUI: a block of lines drawn from a cached grid by a custom element, with the hover, jump and peek gestures resolved to a (line, column) spot from the pointer. Per-row backgrounds and bars come from the two Marks closures, so the listing's selection and anchor bars and the document's slice highlight share it. Width::Wide takes the full width rather than the grid's. It returns the Interaction and the spot under the pointer, whose column is None over the gutter. Shift+wheel over a block whose lines are wider than it scrolls it sideways (kept in the Model's across scrolls, pushed as ScrollAcross), and while it is scrolled a thin weak bar on its left edge shows that the start of the lines is cut off. Which gesture is peek and which is jump comes from keys::code_gesture, that is from the feature registry.

